  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assistance en abris et articles m&#xe9;nagers d&#x2019;urgence et en gestion de sites pour les populations d&#xe9;plac&#xe9;es dans le Nord Kivu</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide emergency Shelter and NFI assistance to displaced, vulnerable people as well as camp management and coordination services. This IOM project provides shelter kits to newly displaced people, and will improve camp coordination management across eight sites in North Kivu. The project provides humanitarian assistance to almost 255,000 people, including 71,300 women, 14,000 children and including 25,500 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
